{{/*
  beads/bootstrap — the "`.beads/` is not initialised, `bd init` it" bootstrap
  step. Kept as its own fragment so every prompt that creates beads shares one
  authoritative bootstrap wording and flow.

  A prompt that creates beads should NOT gate on
  `enabledWhen: ... && DirExists(".beads")`: that hides the prompt in projects
  where beads simply has not been initialised yet, which is precisely the case
  this fragment exists to handle. Gate on `CommandExists("bd")` only, and call
  this fragment at the top of the body. Prompts that operate on an *existing*
  bead (`Item.*` / `Session.BeadsIssue` gates) may keep the `DirExists` gate —
  there is nothing to bootstrap into.

  The fragment renders NOTHING when `.beads/` already exists, so it costs no
  tokens in the common case and needs no "skip this step" wording.

  In a loop conversation it initialises unattended (no question — later
  iterations run with nobody watching); interactively it asks first.

  Usage — at the very top of the body, before any "gather data" steps:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/bootstrap" . }}
*/}}
{{- if not (DirExists ".beads") }}
## Step 0 — Bootstrap beads

Beads (`bd`) is not initialised in this project yet — `.beads/` does not exist.
{{- if .Session.IsLoopConversation }}
Initialise it now, without asking (later iterations of this loop run unattended
and cannot answer a question):

```bash
bd init --non-interactive
```

If `bd init` fails, report the failure and stop.
{{- else }}
Use `mitto_ui_options(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}")` to ask: "Beads is not
initialised in this project yet. Initialise it now?" with options
"Yes — initialise beads" and "No — cancel".

- If the user declines, stop.
- If the user agrees, initialise it non-interactively (it auto-detects a
  sensible default issue prefix from the directory name):

  ```bash
  bd init --non-interactive
  ```

  If the user wants a specific issue ID prefix, pass it explicitly
  (e.g. `bd init --non-interactive --prefix proj`). Then continue.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
